cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Q-Neuro, cite this software release and its falsification manuscript."
title: "Q-Neuro: exact real controls for complex-valued sequential models"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-14
authors:
  - family-names: Shafiee
    given-names: Samyar
repository-code: "https://github.com/Samyrrrrrr990/q-neuro"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - complex-valued neural networks
  - dynamical systems
  - synthetic data
  - exact real controls
  - falsification
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  Q-Neuro is a synthetic, nonclinical framework for testing complex-valued sequential models
  against exact and stronger real-valued controls. The v1.0.0 release reports that an apparent
  complex robustness advantage does not survive the strongest executed real-control envelope; a
  frozen quantitative law also fails held-out transfer, and the grand benchmark remains sealed.
